WEBVTT

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.185
Threat intelligence helps hunters decide where to focus.

00:00:03.185 --> 00:00:07.785
It provides context about adversary behaviors, affected sectors, common objectives,

00:00:07.785 --> 00:00:12.290
technology trends, and observed changes that may be relevant to the organization.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:14.560
Intelligence is most useful when connected to local risk.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:19.070
A report may be important globally but less relevant to the organization's technologies,

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.515
geography, data, customers, or operating model.

00:00:21.515 --> 00:00:25.140
Hunters should evaluate applicability before committing resources.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.529
Behavioral information often has longer value than a single technical indicator.

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:31.895
Understanding the kinds of actions an adversary may attempt can help teams look for

00:00:31.895 --> 00:00:36.120
patterns across different systems even after specific infrastructure or identifiers

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:36.960
change.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.310
Technical indicators can still support focused review, but they require context,

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:42.000
freshness, and validation.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.265
An old or low-confidence indicator should not automatically be treated as proof of harmful

00:00:46.265 --> 00:00:47.425
activity.

00:00:47.425 --> 00:00:51.190
Intelligence can shape a hypothesis by identifying a plausible concern, likely targets,

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.595
expected evidence, and relevant data sources.

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:55.850
The resulting hunt should remain an investigation,

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:58.990
not a predetermined effort to confirm the intelligence report.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:01.665
Local observations also improve intelligence.

00:01:01.665 --> 00:01:05.035
Hunters may learn that a reported behavior is not visible with current telemetry,

00:01:05.035 --> 00:01:07.230
that it appears differently in their environment,

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.295
or that particular systems deserve stronger defensive attention.

00:01:10.295 --> 00:01:13.825
Collaboration among intelligence analysts, hunters, detection engineers,

00:01:13.825 --> 00:01:17.540
incident responders, and system owners creates a useful feedback loop.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.435
External context becomes a local question,

00:01:19.435 --> 00:01:23.130
and local evidence improves future defensive decisions.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:25.515
Intelligence does not guarantee findings or replace telemetry.

00:01:25.515 --> 00:01:29.480
It helps prioritize limited hunting capacity and gives analysts a stronger basis for

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.240
selecting questions that matter to the organization's risk.
